# ============================================================================
# Round-4 C4-7: a checkout may not rewrite the release
# ============================================================================
# This release compares, hashes and executes files as bytes. Every blob in
# supabase/migrations is LF and its statements are fingerprinted by
# scripts/verify-remote-migration-history.mjs against what production actually
# recorded; every shell script under scripts/ and infra/systemd/ is executed by
# bash on the production host; infra/release/release-manifest.json carries
# SHA256 digests of files in this tree. All three are byte-exact claims.
#
# Without the rule below a checkout on a host with the Windows default
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites all of them. Measured on this tree: 126 of 126
# migrations, 29 of 29 scripts/*.sh, 27 of 27 scripts/*.mjs and 5 of 5
# infra/systemd/*.sh come out CRLF, and the content gate then refuses with
# local_content_line_endings. That refusal is correct about the bytes on disk
# and wrong about production, which never applied a CRLF file — a false
# accusation, and one that cannot be cleared by re-running anything.
#
# `eol=lf` makes the checkout write the committed bytes whatever core.autocrlf
# says, so the gate has the release in front of it. The gate's refusal stays
# where it is: it is the defence for a tree that reached the host some other
# way, and removing it would trade a false red for a false green.
#
# tests/release/checkout-byte-fidelity.test.mjs measures this instead of
# reading it, and requires a fresh checkout of HEAD to come out clean.

* text=auto eol=lf

# The four blobs that were committed with mixed line endings before the rule
# above existed. Under `text=auto` alone they would be normalised on the next
# write while `eol=lf` hands their CRLF straight back out, so every working
# tree would report them modified for ever — the same false red, moved. `-text`
# preserves their bytes exactly and reports them clean. Normalising them is a
# content change to files this round does not otherwise touch, so it is not
# done here.
build.log -text
docs/meta-ads-auth-instructions.txt -text
src/app/api/leads/\[id\]/quality/route.ts -text
tests/integration/api-validation-static.test.mjs -text

# This is an authenticated production schema capture whose exact bytes are
# provenance-bound in production-schema-baseline.json. Preserve its original
# whitespace and exempt only that immutable artifact from patch whitespace QA.
supabase/replay/production-schema-baseline.sql whitespace=-trailing-space

# Already classified correctly by `text=auto` (measured: i/-text). Named so a
# future line-ending rule cannot reach them.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.pyc binary
